        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(config): preserve empty env var values in config resolution",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\nFixes two related issues where `resolveConfigValue` / `resolveConfigValueUncached` use `||` (boolean OR) instead of `??` (nullish coalescing), causing an explicitly-set empty environment variable to fall through to the literal config key name.\n\n**Bug 1 — resolver fallback semantics**: When `MY_API_KEY=\"\"`, the `||` operator treats empty string as falsy and returns the literal `\"MY_API_KEY\"` as the API credential. This produces a confusing \"invalid API key\" error from the provider instead of a clear \"not configured\" failure.\n\n**Bug 2 — auth status disagreement**: `ModelRegistry.getProviderAuthStatus` uses a plain truthiness check (`if (process.env[key])`) that treats empty env vars the same as absent env vars. After the `??` fix, the runtime resolver returns `\"\"` (treated as missing auth), but the status path still reports `configured: true, source: \"models_json_key\"`. A custom provider can appear configured in status while runs fail as missing auth.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n- Replaced `||` with `??` in both `resolveConfigValue` and `resolveConfigValueUncached` so that an explicitly-set empty environment variable is preserved rather than silently reinterpreted as a literal config string.\n- Updated `getProviderAuthStatus` to use `in` operator to distinguish \"env var set to empty\" from \"env var not set\", and return `configured: false` when the env var is explicitly empty — aligning status with the runtime resolver.\n\n## User Impact\nUsers who accidentally leave an API key env var set to empty will now get a clear \"API key not configured\" error (both at runtime and in status checks) instead of a confusing \"invalid API key\" error from their provider.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Full-chain proof\nReal environment: Linux x86_64, Node 24. Proof drives production `resolveConfigValue`, `ModelRegistry`, and `AuthStorage` through a temporary `models.json` file on disk — no mocks of tested functions.\n\n```\n[case 1] resolveConfigValue: empty env var with || (pre-fix behavior)\n  ok: || returns key name as value (BUG)\n    buggy result: \"OPENCLAW_PROOF_EMPTY_KEY\" (used as API key!)\n  ok: ?? returns empty string (FIXED)\n    fixed result: \"\"\n  ok: ?? uncached returns empty string (FIXED)\n[case 2] resolveConfigValue: env var set to real key\n  ok: real env value returned correctly\n[case 3] resolveConfigValue: env var not set (literal fallback)\n  ok: missing env falls back to literal key name\n[case 4] ModelRegistry.getProviderAuthStatus: empty env-backed apiKey\n  ok: empty env -> configured: false\n    status: {\"configured\":false}\n  ok: getApiKeyAndHeaders returns empty apiKey (not key name as apiKey)\n    apiKey result: ok=true, apiKey=\"\"\n[case 5] ModelRegistry.getProviderAuthStatus: real env-backed apiKey\n  ok: real env -> configured: true, source: environment\n[case 6] ModelRegistry.getProviderAuthStatus: missing env (literal fallback)\n  ok: missing env -> configured: true, source: models_json_key\n[case 7] ModelRegistry.getProviderAuthStatus: shell command apiKey\n  ok: shell command -> configured: true, source: models_json_command\n\nALL PROOF ASSERTIONS: 10 passed, 0 failed\n```\n\n### Negative control (pre-fix origin/main)\n```\nPre-fix: empty env -> \"OPENCLAW_PROOF_KEY\" <- BUG: returns key name!\nPre-fix uncached: empty env -> \"OPENCLAW_PROOF_KEY\" <- BUG: returns key name!\n---\nFixed: empty env -> \"\" <- FIXED: returns empty string\nFixed uncached: empty env -> \"\" <- FIXED: returns empty string\n```\n\n### vitest (10 tests)\n```\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  10 passed (10)\n```\n\n### Behavior matrix\n| Scenario | Pre-fix resolver | Pre-fix status | Fixed resolver | Fixed status |\n|----------|-----------------|----------------|----------------|--------------|\n| Env = \"sk-real\" | \"sk-real\" | configured: true, env | \"sk-real\" | configured: true, env |\n| Env = \"\" | \"MY_KEY\" (BUG!) | configured: true, models_json_key | \"\" | configured: false |\n| Env absent | \"MY_KEY\" (literal) | configured: true, models_json_key | \"MY_KEY\" (literal) | configured: true, models_json_key |\n",
        "branch": "fix/config-value-empty-env-fallback",
